@startuml
' Traceability:
' - resilient-application-mcp requirements: R5B, R18A-R18F, R19-R28
' - resilient-application-mcp design: bootstrap, local scaffolding, manifest audit
title Bootstrap, Scaffolding, and Local Safety Boundary

skinparam backgroundColor #FFF8EA
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #156B59
  LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #123F37
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #ECFEFF
  ParticipantFontColor #17130F
  BoxBorderColor #CBD5E1
  BoxBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}
skinparam titleFontSize 18
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "Human candidate" as Human
box "Candidate computer (private)" #F8FAFC
participant "Local AI agent" as Agent
participant "Application SOP" as SOP
database "Local application workspace" as Workspace
end box
participant "Public MCP" as MCP

Human -> Agent: Open dedicated folder; paste setup request / guide link
Agent -> Agent: Read public /agent-setup.md over HTTPS
Agent --> Human: Request configuration approval when required
Human -> Agent: Approve within client permission controls
Agent -> Agent: Configure supported MCP client; preserve other settings
opt Client needs reload
  Agent --> Human: Request only required reload; verify after loading
end
alt Modern client
  Agent -> MCP: server/discover
else Legacy client
  Agent -> MCP: initialize + tools/list
end
MCP --> Agent: Public tool contract
break Tools missing or endpoint unreachable
  Agent --> Human: Correct connection address / client settings; retry
end
Agent -> MCP: health
MCP --> Agent: Service identity
Agent -> Workspace: Verify selected writable folder scope (no writes yet)
break Folder missing, read-only or outside selected scope
  Agent --> Human: Open an in-scope folder before local writes
end
Human -> Agent: Run setup prompt after prerequisites pass
Agent -> MCP: Get latest workspace template and application kit
MCP --> Agent: Generic folders, scripts, contracts, version

Agent -> Workspace: Safely scaffold selected root; preserve existing files
Agent -> SOP: strict boot (now executable exists)
note right of Workspace
AGENTS.md, candidate/source,
profile, voice, jobs, applications,
scripts, local SOP state
end note
SOP -> Workspace: Write local state and managed-file hashes
SOP --> Agent: Ready checklist + missing candidate inputs
Agent --> Human: Report readiness; ask for CV or confirmed profile facts

Human -> Workspace: Add private CV, evidence, voice, job files
Agent -> SOP: run local workspace audit
SOP -> Workspace: Build relative-path manifest only
SOP -> MCP: audit_workspace_manifest(manifest)
MCP --> SOP: Current / update guidance
SOP --> Agent: Safe next action; no private file content sent

legend right
MCP supplies generic public resources and reads only the manifest supplied by the local SOP.
Original files remain local; selected writing or CV/JD text can be sent for requested checks later.
Client registration and folder permissions are separate; unresolved prerequisites stop setup.
endlegend

@enduml
